<title>USA: Tenneco unit to buy Polish manufacturer.</title>
<headline>Tenneco unit to buy Polish manufacturer.</headline>
<dateline>DEERFIELD, Ill. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tenneco Inc's Tenneco automotive unit said Tuesday it has agreed to acquire the manufacturing operations of MICHEL, a privately owned, Polish-based manufacturer of replacement market exhaust systems for passenger cars in Eastern Europe.</p>
<p>Terms of the acquisition were not disclosed.</p>
<p>With 60 employees and 1996 sales of nearly $1 million, MICHEL is one of the region's leading manufacturers of replacement exhaust systems for passenger cars built in Eastern Europe, Tenneco said.</p>
<p>Tenneco shares closed down 1/2 at 44-3/8 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
